/**
 * LOCATION / TIME / PICKER ID / AB / AC / AH MAPPER (HEADER-FIXED EDITION)
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------
 * - Dynamically binds to the ACTIVE Google Sheet running the script.
 * - Fixes Time column matching to prevent Box IDs in Column AA.
 * - Processes 400MB+ CSV files via 15MB rolling memory streams.
 * - Implements Primary (box) + Fallback (sorted_box) lookup passes.
 * - Picker ID: fixed-position source columns I (idx 8) and R (idx 17).
 *   R takes priority over I; falls back to I only if R is empty.
 *   Written to destination column AG.
 * - Fixed-position source column U (idx 20) -> destination column AB.
 *   Same primary/fallback keying as everything else.
 * - Destination column AC records which Picker ID source won:
 *   'P&S' if column R had a value (R won), 'PBD' if it fell back to
 *   column I. Written wherever Picker ID itself is written.
 * - NEW: destination column AH records the picker's NAME, looked up
 *   from the 'PICKER DATA' tab (Col A = numeric ID, Col B = FIRST NAME)
 *   in this same spreadsheet. Match is done by stripping any 'ca.'/'CA.'
 *   prefix (and any non-digit chars) off the Picker ID (AG) and off the
 *   PICKER DATA ID column, then comparing the digits. Written wherever
 *   Picker ID itself is written (i.e. in both executeMapping and
 *   executePickerMapping) -- same rule AC already follows.
 * - No date cutoff on source files any more: every file in the Drive folder
 *   is a scan candidate on every run (old box IDs can live in old files).
 *   To keep this fast without a date guess, scanning stops early once every
 *   needed box+fsn key already has a primary match (see scanSourceFiles).
 * - The 10-day tab-selection window in runDaily (which day-tabs get
 *   refreshed) is UNCHANGED -- that's a different concern from file scanning.
 * - BACKFILL_START is now AUTO-DETECTED from the earliest date-named tab
 *   present in this spreadsheet (see getEarliestTabStart). The
 *   CONFIG.BACKFILL_START constant is only a fallback, used if no
 *   date-named tabs exist yet.
 * - executeMapping()      -> writes Location + Time + Picker ID + AB + AC + AH (combined)
 * - executePickerMapping()-> writes Picker ID + AC + AH ONLY, standalone/independent
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------
 */

